Optics, photonics, and laser science (@optics-photonics-and-laser-science: 0, is #chapter, #outline) { r_3G9J2ZB6A56CVVRPPVMES1Y1TS
Optics and photonics study light, its interaction with matter, and its generation, guidance, manipulation, and detection. This material connects rays, imaging, diffraction, polarisation, coherence, spectroscopy, lasers, nonlinear and ultrafast optics, fibres, integrated optics, and optoelectronic devices with precision measurement, communication, fabrication, and the physical limits of optical instruments.

**Common preparation developed:** the [electromagnetic propagation lesson](../core/Connect-electromagnetic-propagation-to-the-shared-wave-and-energy-accounts.lingua) derives a source-free traveling field pair, its constraints, relative field sign and local/slab energy balance from Maxwell equations, reusing the common wave account. It prepares entry without completing optical media, instrumentation, nonlinear optics or full photonics.

**Parent:** [Physics — fields, matter, motion and physical evidence](../Physics.lingua#r_04A5CP8RTBERZEN4XCCDQ3T47W).
} r_3G9J2ZB6A56CVVRPPVMES1Y1TS
